---
import ReferenceTable from '../../components/ReferenceTable.astro';
import Button from '../../components/Button.astro';
import ContentCard from '../../components/ContentCard.astro';
import DatasetNotice from '../../components/DatasetNotice.astro';
import DocumentLayout from '../../layouts/DocumentLayout.astro';
import dataset from '../../../public/dataset/current.json';
import snapshot from '../../../public/review/current/manifest.json';
import validation from '../../../public/review/current/validation.json';
const files = '/review/current';
if (snapshot.dataset.id !== dataset.id) throw new Error('Review and public dataset differ');
---
<DocumentLayout title="Technical review | TENSOR" description="Review the same current public TENSOR dataset used by the graph, profiles and Lab reference investigations." canonicalPath="/review/">
  <ContentCard class="review-package">
    <p class="section-kicker">Current public dataset · Technical review</p>
    <h2>One dataset for exploration, implementation and review.</h2>
    <p>The review package contains the same graph, evidence criteria, event profiles and reference investigations used throughout this site. Reviewers use the public candidate; there is no separate reviewer edition.</p>
    <DatasetNotice />
    <div class="cta-group"><Button variant="primary" href={`${files}/review-package.zip`} download>Download current review package · ZIP</Button><Button variant="secondary" href="/investigations/soc-signin/">Follow the SOC investigation</Button></div>
    <p><a href={`${files}/README.md`}>Review brief</a> · <a href={`${files}/dataset.json`}>Exact dataset inventory</a> · <a href={`${files}/manifest.json`}>Source pins</a> · <a href={`${files}/validation.json`}>Validation results</a> · <a href={`${files}/walkthrough.md`}>First-hour walkthrough</a> · <a href={`${files}/review-form.md`}>Finding form</a></p>
    <h2>Review contents</h2>
    <ReferenceTable label="Current review contents"><thead><tr><th>Artifact</th><th>Scope</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><th>Public graph</th><td>{dataset.counts.questions} questions and {dataset.counts.routes.toLocaleString()} routes across {dataset.counts.domains} domains.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Evidence and event contexts</th><td>Evidence criteria, {dataset.counts.eventProfiles} event profiles and {dataset.counts.qualifiedDefinitions} qualified definitions.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Reference investigations</th><td>{dataset.counts.referenceCases} cross-domain cases, their graph and Lab records, plus the Core binding reference bundles.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Core proposal and binding</th><td>38 logical requirements, binding {dataset.bindingVersion}, unchanged schemas and reference implementation.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Source and checks</th><td>{snapshot.files.length} exact source-file pins, verifier, validation record and finding form.</td></tr>
    </tbody></ReferenceTable>
    <h2>Review workflow</h2>
    <ol><li><strong>Understand:</strong> read <a href="/start/">TENSOR in five minutes</a> and follow the SOC investigation into the graph and Lab.</li><li><strong>Challenge meaning:</strong> examine the <a href="/questions/">question catalog</a>, evidence criteria and <a href="/graphs/review/">item-level review</a>. Check unknowns, bounded negative findings, multiple routes and cross-domain leads.</li><li><strong>Check layers:</strong> inspect <a href="/extensions/">vendor and organization additions</a> without changing public question meaning or treating policy as an investigative fact.</li><li><strong>Exchange:</strong> independently read, export and reimport cases; report preserved, unsupported and lost meaning.</li><li><strong>Return findings:</strong> cite the dataset digest, exact question/profile/requirement, reproduction and untested scope.</li></ol>
    <h2>Reproduce the same source</h2>
    <p>Extract the ZIP into an empty directory. Verify its source archive before extraction, then verify the extracted files. The package uses Node.js 24.21.0 and Python 3.11 or later.</p>
    <pre><code>{`python3 verify-snapshot.py
python3 verify-snapshot.py /absolute/path/to/extracted-source
cd /absolute/path/to/extracted-source
npm ci
npm run check
node scripts/build_dataset.mjs --check
python3 -m unittest discover -s tests/legacy -q
python3 scripts/verify_semantic_review.py
python3 scripts/evaluate_entry_scenarios.py`}</code></pre>
    <p>The <a href={`${files}/validation.json`}>validation record</a> contains observed commands, environment and limits. Its {validation.checks.find(c=>c.nodeTests)?.nodeTests} Node tests and {validation.checks.find(c=>c.tests)?.tests} Python regressions are author-side checks. Separate implementations, authenticated field evidence and institutional approval remain external evaluation work.</p>
    <h2>Findings and stewardship</h2>
    <p><a href="/governance/">Current stewardship</a> and the <a href="/docs/review-process.md">finding process</a> cover responses and dissent. Review participation is not endorsement. Public reports use fictional or authorized material; sensitive vulnerabilities use <a href="https://github.com/TENSOR-Standards-Consortium/TENSOR-Framework/security/advisories/new">private reporting</a>.</p>
    <div class="cta-group"><Button variant="primary" href="https://github.com/TENSOR-Standards-Consortium/TENSOR-Framework/issues/new?template=implementation-report.yml">Technical finding</Button><Button variant="secondary" href="/archives/">Historical archives</Button></div>
    <details><summary>Exact source and dataset identity</summary><p>Dataset: <code>{dataset.id}</code></p><p>Source: <a href={`${snapshot.sourceRepository}/tree/${snapshot.sourceCommit}`}><code>{snapshot.sourceCommit}</code></a>. Generated review packaging is excluded from its own source archive to avoid recursion.</p></details>
  </ContentCard>
</DocumentLayout>
<style>.review-package { overflow-wrap:anywhere; } .review-package pre { overflow-wrap:normal; }</style>
